<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>

<!--
  OVERLAY (2026-09-01).  THE POINT OF THE `nnpdf` CONFIG IS TO CHANGE THE
  PARTON DISTRIBUTION, AND WITHOUT THIS FILE IT DID NOT CHANGE IT FOR CHARM.

  `genie/config/nnpdf/BYPDF.xml` substitutes NNPDF4.0 into the Bodek-Yang
  model, which is what the INCLUSIVE deep-inelastic cross-section is built
  from.  But G18_02a computes charm deep-inelastic scattering with a
  DIFFERENT algorithm.  ModelConfiguration.xml maps
  `XSecModel@genie::EventGenerator/DIS-CC-CHARM` to
  `genie::AivazisCharmPXSecLO/CC-Default`, and that algorithm carries its OWN
  `PDF-Set` parameter, hardwired to `genie::GRV98LO/Default` in the stock
  configuration.  It never consults BYPDF.

  So the "NNPDF4.0" variant was an NNPDF4.0 INCLUSIVE sample whose CHARM was
  still GRV98.  The symptom: its charm cross section sat on top of the GRV98
  tune's to better than a per cent while the inclusive rate moved by five,
  which the user flagged as implausible, since the two sets differ most in
  exactly the STRANGENESS that drives the s to c conversion.

  Keep the `CC-Default` param_set name.  ModelConfiguration.xml names that
  set explicitly, so an overlay under any other name is loaded and ignored.
  Keep `Default` too: `CC-Default` inherits Charm-Mass and the CKM elements
  from it through CommonParam, and a file with only `CC-Default` aborts with
  "Key: Charm-Mass does not exist".

  NOTE FOR EDITORS: no double hyphen may appear anywhere in an XML comment.
  The first version of this file used them as dashes in the prose; GENIE
  refused the whole file, fell back with no charm configuration at all and
  aborted.  It failed loudly, which is the one good thing about it.
-->

<alg_conf>

  <param_set name="Default">
     <param type="string" name="CommonParam"> CKM,Masses </param>
  </param_set>

  <param_set name="CC-Default">
     <param type="alg" name="PDF-Set">         genie::LHAPDF6/NNPDF40_nnlo_0 </param>
     <param type="alg" name="XSec-Integrator"> genie::DISXSec/Default        </param>
  </param_set>

</alg_conf>
